velazquez-de-cuellar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar was a Spanish conquistador who led the conquest of Cuba from 1511 and became its first governor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dieric-bouts"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dieric-bouts.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dieric Bouts</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Dieric Bouts was an Early Netherlandish painter, born in Haarlem around 1415, who worked in Leuven from the 1440s and became its official city painter in 1468.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diessenhofen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diessenhofen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diessenhofen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Diessenhofen is a small town in the Swiss canton of Thurgau on the south bank of the Rhine, between Schaffhausen and Stein am Rhein.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-porvoo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diet-of-porvoo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diet of Porvoo</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Diet of Porvoo was the assembly of the four estates of Finland that met at Porvoo in 1809, during the Finnish War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-schwabisch-hall"><span class="enc-name">Diet of Schwäbisch Hall</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Diet of Schwäbisch Hall was an imperial assembly held in 1190 at Schwäbisch Hall in Swabia under King Henry VI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/d